    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-direction-extended-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Recognize common extended directional meanings",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Interpret the whole learned predicate: 想起来 or 想起 can bring a thought back to mind, without literal upward movement. 下去 can extend an activity forward in time, as in continuing to speak; it need not describe descent.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我想起来了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ xiǎng qǐlái le 。",
                "meaning": "I remember now.",
                "audio": "12b5c5fcc07c320a940c11bb010f4d06de4ce0eef23308b155e4ee2627dce1a4"
              },
              {
                "text": "我想起他的名字了。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ xiǎngqǐ tā de míngzi le 。",
                "meaning": "I recalled his name.",
                "audio": "5df01116fe9f7e47bdd5f67b0442023740f0c1250bf5e524dba7edcc051f7a69"
              },
              {
                "text": "我们继续说下去。",
                "pinyin": "wǒmen jìxù shuō xiàqù 。",
                "meaning": "We continue speaking.",
                "audio": "2c1437bf9a93da9055fb0a19e5260ec2690c334f52ea8ab54b750daed28637bf"
              }
            ]
          },
